        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Organizations: Little River Railroad, Southern Railway System\n- Places: Maryville, Elkmont, Tennessee, valley, Chilhowee Inn\n- Concepts: class III railroad, logging town, resort community, pioneer Appalachian community\n\nFacts:\n- The Little River Railroad was a historic class III railroad that operated between Maryville and Elkmont, Tennessee, from 1901 to 1939.\n- The valley in Elkmont, Tennessee, has been home over time to a pioneer Appalachian community, a logging town, and a resort community.\n- Chilhowee Inn was the last stop of the Knoxville and Augusta line of the Southern Railway System and the starting point for the Little River Railroad.",
